Legend:
r.*: Receiver*
s.*: Sender*
.bn: BlockNumber/BlockInstance "BlockName"
 - BlockNumber is the type of block.
 - BlockInstance is the instance Id for the block. Together with nodeId and
   BlockNumber it will uniquely identify a block. Will not be printed for packed
   signals.
 - BlockName describes the type of block. It's a function of BlockNumber.
.nodeId: Node ID.
.sigId: Sequence number for signal, applied at the receiving side.
.gsn: GlobalSignalNumber, the type of signal.
.sn: "SignalName"
  SignalName describes the type of signal. For non-packed signals it's a
  function of GlobalSignalNumber. Packed signals don't have a
  GlobalSignalNumber.
.threadId: The thread Id.
  Will only be printed for local (same-node) signals.
.threadSigId: Sequence number for local (same-node) signals. Will only be
  incremented for JBB priority signals. Will only be printed for local
  (same-node) signals.
prio: Priority for signal.
  JBA = High priority
  JBB = Normal priority
length: Number of Uint32 words in signal payload
trace: Trace number between 0-63
#sec: Number of sections in signal
fragInfo: Details about signal fragmentation.
  0 = Not fragmented
  1 = First fragment
  2 = Fragment other than first or last
  3 = Last fragment
